==Matches==
A draw was held on 17 November in [[Nagoya]] (Japan) to decide the "positions" of the three teams entering the quarter-finals: [[Al Sadd SC|Al-Sadd]] ([[Asian Football Confederation|AFC]]), [[Espérance Sportive de Tunis|Espérance de Tunis]] ([[Confederation of African Football|CAF]]), and [[C.F. Monterrey|Monterrey]] ([[CONCACAF]]).<ref>{{cite news |title=Teams react to Japan 2011 draw |url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/newsid=1544241/index.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111120005101/http://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/newsid=1544241/index.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=20 November 2011 |publisher=FIFA |date=17 November 2011 |access-date=2 August 2012 }}</ref>

If a match was tied after normal playing time:<ref name="regulations"/>
*For elimination matches, [[Overtime (sports)#Association football|extra time]] would be played. If still tied after extra time, a [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalty shoot-out]] would be held to determine the winner.
*For the matches for fifth place and third place, no extra time would be played, and the match would go straight to a penalty shoot-out to determine the winner.

